{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1794001476,"nonce":"tHZyDuhIuuXToI/aVz2ay2DB7rA=","title":"Run the book web examples in the worker runner the component page uses","message":"Book examples (/docs/examples/\u003cname\u003e/) start through a generated #[wasm_bindgen(start)] shim that calls WebApp::run_with_async_setup on the page's main thread. Compiling a 10-16 MB module, decoding assets and uploading GPU textures all block the browser main thread, so heavy demos load slowly and can stall the page. The component page already avoids this: web/components/runtime/host.js transfers the canvas to a dedicated worker (OffscreenCanvas) and worker.js drives a WebApp::new_offscreen runtime. See 784ab13.\n\nObserved 2026-11-06 on blinc.rs after the Cloudflare move: strangler_demo renders in headless Chrome (Metal WebGPU), but the owner reports it does not load and the heavy demos load slowly.\n\nPlan\n- tools/build-web-examples emits a worker entry beside the existing start shim: an exported create_runtime(canvas, width, height, dpr) that applies the same setup (theme init, fonts, asset preload) and set_ui_builder(build_ui) on WebApp::new_offscreen, plus frame/input/resize/dispose exports matching the catalog runtime.\n- Generalise runtime/worker.js and host.js so the module URL and the runtime constructor come from boot options, not the fixed blinc_component_demos module.\n- Example pages load through the host: start on visit, report progress, first frame and errors, keep a visible fallback when OffscreenCanvas or worker WebGPU is unavailable (main-thread path stays as a separate, reported fallback).\n- The asset remap shim patches window.fetch only; the worker needs the same remap (self.fetch) or the manifest passed in boot options.\n- Cover text input/IME, clipboard, media and keyboard through the existing host bridges; list examples that need DOM-only services and keep them on the main-thread path until bridged.\n- Browser check on dedicated pages, strangler_demo first, then a sweep of all 48.\n\nSide finding: .wasm objects on assets.blinc.rs report cf-cache-status DYNAMIC (not edge-cached; .bin and images are HIT). A cache rule for the asset host would fix that; needs a token with Cache Rules edit.","files":null}]}